    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7420399888695218178",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7420399888695218178/",
    "text": "Thank you for the great feedback Tuberizer.com! A few people have asked how I actually built it, so here’s some tips on the workflow: \n\nIt’s not difficult, but the process really matters. The tools have come a long way. The mistake most people make is trying to one-shot an app in Lovable. That never works.\n\nWhat does work is using ChatGPT first to get everything out of your head - ideas, goals, constraints, and rough features. I’d strongly recommend doing this by voice.\n\nTreat it like you’re talking to an experienced app developer and let it challenge and refine your thinking.\n\nOnce that’s done, ask ChatGPT to turn all of that into a series of staged prompts for Lovable. That sequencing is key.\n\nA rough structure looks like this:\n\nPrompt 1 - Foundations:\nDescribe what the app is meant to become, its scope, and the end goal. Ask Lovable to build a clean baseline structure and tech stack. No features yet.\n\nPrompt 2 - Content:\nAdd content next. Placeholders are fine at this stage. The goal is to get everything rendering cleanly and logically.\n\nPrompt 3+ - Features (one at a time):\nLayer features gradually. Trying to do too much in one go is where things usually break.\n\nOnce the core structure is in place, that’s where it gets fun. \n\nYou can start experimenting and having real conversations with Lovable about what’s easy to add, what’s risky, and how to approach more complex pieces safely.\n\nIn my case, that meant integrating multiple APIs, pulling in video thumbnails, fetching transcripts from a separate service, and summarising them in a very specific way.\n\nOne trick is simply asking Lovable what it would suggest as an expert app and web designer, and then choosing which ideas to implement and in what order.\n\nBest advice I can give: treat it like a human. Give context. Be verbose. Explain the vision. Ask for advice along the way. \n\nIt genuinely feels like working with a small team of AI agents moving at lightning speed.\n\nThis is a real glimpse of where things are heading. If you’ve been curious but hesitant, I’d highly recommend giving it a proper try.",
    "date": "1 month ago",
    "likes": 25,
    "comments": 19,
    "impressions": 774,
