    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7419317783114473472",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7419317783114473472/",
    "text": "🔥 I'm so excited to launch my first fully Vibe Coded app! 🔥 \"Tuberizer\" gives you concise summaries of your favourite YouTube channels  so you know what’s worth watching.\n\nThe problem was simple. I follow so many AI and tech YouTube channels, and I just can’t keep up. Videos are 30–60 minutes long, and too often you only realise halfway through that it wasn’t worth the time.\n\nI wanted a place where I could browse the channels I follow, quickly read what each video actually covers, and decide whether it’s worth watching. Or just skim the latest videos in a channel to see the news, themes, and key takeaways. That didn’t exist, so I built it.\n\nTuberizer allows you to get the key findings and takeaways in a few minutes rather than watching many hours of videos .\n\nI actually tried to build this six months ago. The tech wasn’t there, and even paying someone to build it failed. This time, I built the entire thing myself in a weekend. Zero coding - all natural language prompts.\n\nTuberizer covers a wide range of channels across AI, tech, podcasts, documentaries, politics, and more. If your favourite channel isn’t listed, you can paste in any channel or video and generate a clean, shareable summary link. It’s perfect for sending someone a video without asking them to blindly commit to an hour-long watch.\n\nI had a lot of fun building this. If it gets traction, I’ll add more advanced features like a daily email digest of new videos from your favourite channels, custom prompts, playlist integration, and collective summaries showing what entire categories like AI have been talking about over the past week.\n\nLink is in the comments. Would love to hear what you think and would really appreciate any likes, comments and shares!",
    "date": "1 month ago",
    "likes": 119,
