    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7419003016076238849",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7419003016076238849/",
    "text": "I just vibe coded an app in a weekend, that’s far better than what a developer charged me thousands to build and failed. 🤯\n\nStory time:\n\nThis was an idea I’d had for ages. I wanted to solve a problem I had for ages and knew others would appreciate the solution also. \n\nI spoke to a few developers, I was quoted between $10k and $30k, which felt like too big a gamble for a random idea, so I parked it.\n\nWhen Lovable first came out, I tried to build it myself, but it failed, the app was still too complex for it to achieve properly on such a platform.\n\nI asked on some 'vibe coding' forums if I was doing something wrong or how I could achieve this, and got laughed at.\n\nMultiple people told me you’d never build something like this with vibe coding tools.\n\nOne person reached out and offered to build it properly using a traditional full stack approach. He had some spare time and needed the money, so did me a special deal for a few thousand dollars, a fraction of what it usually cost, so I did it. \n\nNearly three months later, what I got back wasn’t up to scratch. It just wasn't something I would feel comfortable launching. \n\nIt didn’t look great, had a few bugs and wasn't implemented exactly the way I asked for, I'd paid him the last payment and couldn't get him to do any more. \n\nNot great, but you get what you pay for I suppose 🤷‍♂️ \n\nI tried to plug in some vibe coding tools to try to fix it but could not figure it out so I parked it. Oh well. \n\nSo, this weekend, several months later, I decided to try again using Lovable. \n\nThe tools have improved a lot, so I wanted to see what was possible. \n\nTo my surprise, it worked! I had a solid version working in a couple of hours. Incredible! \n\nIt also looked way better, operated smoother, and I could design it exactly the way I want on the fly. This is the future. \n\nThings like connecting APIs and managing larger volumes of data, images and video that failed before, just worked this time. \n\nI then added a bunch of extra features I’d never even attempted, mostly by asking the tool how it would improve the product and saying yes to the best ideas. \n\nIt's amazing. I'm astonished at what you can do on the fly and how much better it now is. \n\nThe models seem to have really turned corner now. It's unbelievably impressive what is possible by just asking for it in natural language, letting AI figure out the rest.\n\nIt's almost as if I have a developer at the end of my phone who I voice dictate my instructions to, and a minute or two later the new features are available in the app. \n\nIt really is like magic.\n\nI’m being deliberately vague about the product but I'm going to reveal it here tomorrow. \n\nAnd a have a favour to ask:\n\nI'd really love your support with a like and a comment tomorrow to help spread it far and wide. Pls like or comment and I'll send it to you to test❣️ \n\nI genuinely think this will be useful to a lot of people, and I’m excited to hear what you think, and see where it goes.",
