    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7368891093758660608",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7368891093758660608/",
    "text": "RIP Photoshop!! And many other apps too... This is \"Nano Banana\" from Google DeepMind. It does in seconds with a text - what used to take an expert hours, days or more.\n\nThis is the AI Effect - it democratises skills across the board—and it's kinda scary when you think about it.\n\nPeople would have paid hundreds of thousands, if not million,s to pull off these kind of effects in the past.\n\nRemember the faces morphing together in Michael Jackson’s \"It Don’t Matter If You’re Black or White\" video? That cost $5m. Or the T1000 getting shot and melting in Terminator 2? That cost $4m.\n\nNow the same effects can be achieved for just a few dollars.\n\nI would not want to be a Hollywood special effects artist right now.\n\nWithin two years, kids will be making movies in their bedrooms, which would have taken a $100m budget just a few years ago...",
