    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7324331743262511104",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7324331743262511104/",
    "text": "Want a guaranteed way to get rich, without having to have a very high income or exit a startup?\n\nAgainst all odds, there are several stories of people becoming very wealthy despite having very basic jobs, but they became very wealthy with just consistent investing and understanding the laws of compound interest:\n\n1. Ronald Read – Janitor & Gas Station Attendant\n\nWorked his whole life as a janitor and gas station attendant, yet died in 2014 with a $8 million fortune.\nHe lived frugally, invested in blue-chip dividend stocks for decades, and reinvested everything—proving discipline beats income.\nLegacy: Donated most of his wealth to his local library and hospital.\n\n2. Grace Groner – Secretary at Abbott Labs\n\nBought $180 of Abbott stock in 1935 while working as a secretary and held it for 75 years—worth $7 million by the time she died.\nShe never chased trends, just reinvested dividends and stayed the course.\nLegacy: Left everything to a scholarship fund.\n\n\n3. Anne Scheiber – IRS Auditor\n\nDespite never earning more than $3,150 a year, she turned $5,000 into $22 million by the time she died at 101.\nShe invested in quality stocks, held for the long term, and reinvested religiously.\nLegacy: Donated her entire fortune to fund scholarships for women.\n\n\n4. Sylvia Bloom – Legal Secretary\n\nSpent 67 years as a legal secretary in NYC and quietly mirrored the investments of lawyers she worked with—leaving behind $9 million.\nShe saved consistently, invested wisely, and never changed her modest lifestyle.\nLegacy: Donated most of her estate to education.\n\n\n5. Theodore Johnson – UPS Employee\n\nWorked in UPS’s payroll department and never earned more than a modest salary—yet built a $70 million fortune.\nHe invested 20% of every paycheck in UPS stock and let it grow over decades.\nLegacy: Gave away much of his wealth to educational causes.\n\n\nThere is, of course, another way.\n\n\nhashtag\n#studybitcoin",
