    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7327994655923474433/",
    "text": "Has anyone noticed a very significant falloff in views and engagement on your posts lately? \n\nI'm not sure what's going on with the algo but the numbers are way way down to what they used to be last year.\n\nIt's pretty frustrating to spend an hour researching and writing a post for the algo to only show it to a few hundred people, especially when I have almost 25k followers - they only show a post of to a small single digit % of them.\n\nI used to always get 3-5k views and generally 10k+ if it did well, now, crickets?\n\nLike many on this site - we have spent years creating content - which Linkedin monetises - unlike other platforms like X we don't see any of it, and many of us are even paying for the privilege with Premium.\n\nI did take a break for a while over xmas and posted a lot less often for a while after - the Algo seems to publish you if you are not perfectly consistent. Seems a little unfair when we all have to juggle and day job and family. Like a cruel drug lol.\n\nIs there any point any more? Has anyone noticed the same?",
