    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7298267749712121856",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7298267749712121856/",
    "text": "Remember when Elon announced XAI and everybody laughed at the thought he could ever compete with Open AI? I said at the time 'never underestimate Elon' - and he's done it again.\n\nGrok 3 just topped almost all the benchmarks across the board - lightning fast, great reasoning, coding and deep research, all in a fraction of the time, team and resources.\n\nWhat's important to note here is that not only have they caught up fast, but also where their trajectory is going. Elon said last week that he thinks this is the last time Grok will be behind any AI - that's a big claim.\n\nNot only is it the best model in the world, but it also has direct access to the number 1 news source in the world.\n\nI never believed Elon when he said that he was buying Twitter to protect free speech - in my opinion, it was always about the data - there is no better data source that X.\n\nHe also managed to build the biggest compute cluster in the world. Firstly, it was thought by most that it was impossible to make more than 30,000 GPU's work together coherently, but his first principles approach solved this.\n\nNot only this, but the entire project took 122 days from start to finish. NVidia CEO Jensen Huang said that xAI’s feat of going from hardware setup to training in 19 days was \"superhuman,\" usually this would take about a year.\n\nThere is an ongoing discussion around 'scaling rates' which wonders how far we can keep going by simply growing the size of the clusters and getting the same or growing rates of improvement of LLM models.\n\nMany claimed this would peak by now, but so far we are not seeing any ceiling.\n\nMy belief here is that not only is this true, but we are going to see significant efficiency gains along the way also - this was clearly proven by DeepSeek's recent announcements. \n\nElon is planning to double the size of the cluster to 200,000 GPU's - upgrading from H100s to H200's. Things will only accelerate from here.\n\nThe other important thing to note is how Grok has a personality. I love ChatGPT and it's still my go-to - mainly because of the locking of it having all the data I put in over years that is not easily portable - but I still feel it's a little bland and stale.\n\nWhat I have been waiting for for ages is a real personality in AI - and even a set of different personalities. Just like you would go to different people to ask different questions, not because of their knowledge but because of the type of answer you are looking for - that is what will come next.\n\nGrok will soon release Voice Mode. I was so excited about OpenAI's voice mode but I was quite disappointed as it did not speak conversationally like a human, it was more speaking the output of a text LLM - there's a clear difference.\n\nIt won't be long before we are chatting to Grok in our Tesla's and also with the Tesla Optimus Robot.\n\nThe real winner of the battle between the big AI giants is us, the user. The cost of intelligence is trending to zero and that will bring incredible things for humanity.",
    "date": "1 year ago",
    "likes": 54,
    "comments": 96,
    "impressions": 20439,
    "_debug": ""
