    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7268237447401033728",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7268237447401033728/",
    "text": "Are salespeople close to being replaced by AI?\n\nMy career was born in sales, it did it for over a decade. Picking up the phone cold calling all day is a hard job.\n\nWe are now getting to the stage where AI can have some pretty convincing conversations, and it's only going to get better from here.\n\nWill it replace a full salesperson from start to finish? No, not any time soon.\n\nBut imagine being able to deploy a swarm of ai appointment setters at a moments notice, and have them A/B test different approaches.\n\nOutsourcing the tedious part of demand generation could be a game changer for startup trying to get off the ground. \n\nI'm dying to try it myself. \n\nHowever, I fear the amount of sales calls we receive will skyrocket.\n\nMaybe we'll just have another AI to screen the calls for us?\n\nWhere do we think this is going?",
    "date": "1 year ago",
    "likes": 38,
    "comments": 21,
    "impressions": 4327,
    "_debug": ""
