    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7264959369853689856",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7264959369853689856/",
    "text": "Forget \nhashtag\n#NVIDIA, the hottest stock right now is \nhashtag\n#Microstrategy - Michael Saylor's spectacular success up 775% in a year by implementing a \nhashtag\n#BitcoinStrategicReserve. Unlike NVidia, this is only getting going...\n\nSaylor came from MIT as a systems engineer and started Microstrategy over 20 years ago - one of the longest running CEO's in tech.\n\nAfter the crash of '99 the stock never recovered - until he made the decision to become a 'Bitcoin Company'.\n\nMichaels's strategy is simple. They started spending any money they had in the company on Bitcoin - to hold on the balance sheet and never sell.\n\nThey then started selling shares, diluting the stock but buying Bitcoin - a far harder and better-performing asset. \n\nInitially, Bitcoin was in a bear market and they were $5 Billion under water - but he was never worried. He said he'll be 'Buying the Top Forever'\n\nThen he started taking out extensive loans at extremely low interest rates below 1% - to buy more Bitcoin.\n\nEventually, the Bitcoin price recovered and now he's over $12 Billion in profit.\n\nHe actually uses leverage and has gained over 20% net extra bitcoin for his shareholders.\n\nMichael just announced he is going to raise $42 Billion more in the next 2 years. $21m in share dilution and $21m in bonds and loans.\n\nHe just announced the largest share dilution in history - which for any other company would tank the stock completely - but in fact, the stock rose slightly on the news.\n\nIn this video he shares his thoughts on some saying his stock trades at a premium to Bitcoin - and as always he gives a masterful answer.\n\nHis long-term plan is to turn Microstrategy into a \"Bitcoin Bank'. He's advising other companies like Microsoft and even governments to do the same. \n\nConsidering he's just turned his stock into the best-performing on the S&P - I think quite a few will listen to him.\n\nThe benefit of MSTR as that it acts as a proxy to Bitocin or those who cannot buy directly - like pension funds etc who can't buy Bitcoin directly, but can buy equities.\n\nThis is \nhashtag\n#notfinancialadvice but I just changed my pension into 'self-directed' and put a chunk of it in \nhashtag\n#MSTR \nhashtag\n#toptip\n\nMSTR is going to become one of the biggest companies in the world - that's my prediction.\n\nMany more companies are going to take a similar stance - along with governments and sovereign wealth funds.\n\nIf you are pissed you missed Nvidia, I suggest you take a look into Microstrategy.\n\n\nhashtag\n#notfinancialadvice",
