    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7256663366402764800",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7256663366402764800/",
    "text": "Tesla absolutely CRUSHED their earnings last week, and the stock has soared nearly 23%. Here's why:\n\n\nhashtag\n#Tesla has now proven they can produce electric vehicles at very high margin, while the rest of the auto industry is making a loss on every vehicle sold.\n\nYes, a loss - and some hefty ones too. Mercedes, GM, VW, Jaguar - are all losing a fortune per vehicle sold.\n\nFor example, \"Ford’s electric vehicle unit reported that losses soared in the first quarter to $1.3 billion, or $132,000 for each of the 10,000 vehicles it sold in the first three months of the year\".\n\nTesla announced they are already profitable on each Cybertruck, while Ford are Losing $60,000 per F1 Lightening.\n\nYikes.\n\nElon has always said that Tesla's competitive advantage will be in it's manufacturing ability. \"The machine that builds the machine\".\n\nThey lowered their Cost of Good Sold to the lowest levels ever despite huge investments in infrastructure and AI.\n\nElon built the \"Supercluster' of 100,000 Nvidia H100's in 6 weeks - that would usually take a year. This means they are 'no longer compute constrained' - which is big news for FSD.\n\nFull Self Driving, which has been promised imminently for many years, really is around the corner - target Q2 next year for the first trial cities.. Several million vehicles are ready to become autonomous taxis netting Tesla a profit on each ride. Look out Uber.\n\nAnd they have not even introduced automation via humanoid robots yet. Elon said that Optimus is going to be their most profitable product, and possibly the most profitable product ever.\n\nWall Street have not even woken up to this yet.\n\nBut it's not just that. The Tesla Semi is ramping up with a new dedicated Nevada factory and once it does - the TAM in the trucking market is astronomical.\n\nThe Energy Storage business also had strong growth with over 30% margins.\n\nThey also increased their free cashflow by $2.7 Billion to a whopping $33 Billion.\n\nThey are producing the Model 3 cheaper than ever and passing those savings along to the customer - the only company continually cutting the prices of their cars.\n\nDue to sustained high interest rates some people are putting off new car purchases. The media is pedalling lesser demand for EV's - but what they are not showing is the lower demand for ICE (petrol) vehicles.\n\nIn china, the worlds biggest and most forward looking car market, ICE vehicle sales are collapsing.\n\nIs this the canary in the coalmine? Have we reached \"Peak ICE\"?\n\nOnly Tesla and a few of the Chinese companies can produce EV's profitably - but even at that most of them are backed by the CCP.\n\nTesla have now shown they can do what everyone said was impossible. strong growth, exceptional margins, the best production automation - and we have not even seen the results of the colossal potential for FSD, Robotaxis, Semi, Energy and Optimus.\n\nElon said \"My prediction is that Tesla will become the most valuable company of all time\"\n\nWould you bet against Elon?",
