    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7243953389749825537",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7243953389749825537/",
    "text": "This is incredible!!! You can now turn any document or file - into a podcast! It's called Google NotebookLM and it's like your \"virtual research assistant\". I really love this!\n\nIn this example, they take a highly technical and extremely complicated (aka boring) research paper, and turn it into an easy-to-understand and consume conversation between two (AI) people, in podcast format.\n\nThis is game-changing.\n\nI just tried it with my own company's white paper, and learned some things I didn't even know! It summarised and described certain parts better than I could - and I consider this one of my strengths.\n\nThink about the implications for areas like research and education. Be it kids, college students or professionals, you now have the ability for AI to effectively teach you anything with an audio summary as a podcast conversation.\n\nThis podcast feature is just one part of NotebookLM - it actually does much more. It acts as a 'personalized AI collaborator', helping you better understand, organize, and refine ideas based on any set of uploaded documents. \n\nRight now it spits out an audio file but you know what's coming next - you'll be able to have an actual conversation with it and interrupt and ask questions at any stage.\n\nAI is about to disrupt education forever.\n\nSocrates was taught by Plato, Alexander the Great was taught by Aristotle.\nSoon all kids will have their own world-class expert in the form of AI.",
    "date": "1 year ago",
    "likes": 60,
    "comments": 40,
    "impressions": 6724,
    "_debug": ""
