    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7221528547381624833",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7221528547381624833/",
    "text": "Want to know the future of Software?? Input > Neural Net > Output. That's it.\n\nWe are going to enter the era of 'software on demand'. No need for specific software applications, we ask the AI for what we want and we get it. Wild.\n\nOf course this is a very very long way away, but we will start to see glimpses of it with AI agents doing the work for us, saving us time and taking some of our workload away.\n\nIt will mean we won't have to learn how to use complex software processes and techniques - the AI will do most of the work for you.\n\nIt's like how you can now easily make a fantastical image with AI that previously would have taken years of experience and significant skills in photoshop to achieve.\n\nTalent and skills are slowly being democratised. \n\nWe've already seen AI build super simple applications like a calculator or the game of Snake. Just imagine what will be possible in 5 years.\n\nEventually AI will be able to design an entire app for you on demand for a single use. It's crazy to think how this will disrupt the SaaS market, developers and the industry as a whole.\n\nThey used to say 'Software is eating the world' - I think AI is about to eat Software...",
    "date": "1 year ago",
    "likes": 13,
    "comments": 7,
    "impressions": 1764,
    "_debug": ""
