    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7208074330927235072/",
    "text": "The Chinese have entered the AI race! This is Kling, China's version of Open Ai's Sora - and while it's probably not quite as good, the chinese do have one major advantage...\n\nIn the upcoming AI race, China may be behind technologically - however they do have a significant competitive edge due to the country’s lax stance on copyright laws.\n\nUnlike most companies which at least have to try to abide by intellectual property regulations, China can train its AI models on a vast array of data, as they are mostly indifferent to ownership. \n\nAdditionally, China has been collecting extensive data on its billion-plus population for many years, providing a vast and rich dataset for AI training.\n\nWith AGI and ASI being the holy grail and probably not more than 5-7 years away - nations are going to be in hot competition to get there first.",
