    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7189233341353623552",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7189233341353623552/",
    "text": "Meta just announced their new AI powered Ray-Ban glasses, and the examples of what they can now do are pretty fantastic.\n\nI'm a big fan of any device that lowers our reliance on a smartphone, and I think these solve lots of small problems and also bring in some interesting new capabilities.\n\nApart from listing to music or podcasts, taking photos, videos and live streaming, the ability to dictate whatsapp messages or even send voice notes will be super useful - and this is just the beginning. We'll soon see a lot more of the ability to interact with other applications just with our voice.\n\nHaving an AI Assistant in / above your ear via a pair of smart glasses is definitely the way to go and once the capabilities mature, I believe this is going to grow significantly\n\nYes the Apple Vision Pro is cool but in reality no one wants a brick on their face, and Apple are already scaling back forecasts on the device as people realise it's cool for a few minutes, but just not suitable for long term usage.\n\nAI powered wearables such as smart glasses are going to take off in the next year or so, I can't wait to get my hands on a pair!\n\nBut just wait until they get video! Then things will get really interesting...",
