    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7167514726522933249",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7167514726522933249/",
    "text": "hashtag\n#NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang thinks that soon we won't need programmers anymore, because with AI, everybody will be a programmer. \n\nNow domain experts across the spectrum will be able to build software just by instructing an AI in normal language.\n\nAI is breaking down the technical barriers, democratising software development.\n\nThis will lead to a new era of \nhashtag\n#innovation, where ideas matter more than coding skills.\n\nIt will drastically reduce the time it takes to develop software and we'll have personalised and niche applications, tailored to our specific needs.\n\nDon't like the way an app looks or operates? Just ask and it will change it to your liking on the fly. \n\nIt will lead to a new era of hyper personalisation, market differention and enhanced customer experience. \n\nSo is this the end for programmers? \n\nI don't think so. Writing code is only a small part of their job. \n\nThey'll climb up the value chain and focus on bigger more important tasks like architecture, security and integration. \n\nProgrammers will pivot towards the need for a deep understanding of business processes, strategy, and user experience design. \n\nThe way things are done is going to change so much that in 5 years, we'll probably look back on today like the technological dark ages.",
