    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7117780885378072576",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7117780885378072576/",
    "text": "hashtag\n#Bitcoin. It's over. It's finished. The Game is up. Bitcoin has already won. There are no credible critics left. \n\nYesterday Fidelity Investments, who manage over 4 Trillion dollars, released their \"Bitcoin First Revisitied report.\n\nHere's the 23 page report summarised in the most important quotes and takeaways:\n\n📍 The invention of the wheel represented an entirely new technology that, once invented, could never be reinvented. Similarly, never in human history had the problem of peer-to-peer electronic cash been solved until Bitcoin.\n📍 The internet protocol suite known as TCP/ IP is an open-source base layer...applications on top of which to be built.\" Owning Bitcoin would be akin to being able to own the base layer of the Internet\"\n📍 Bitcoin is best understood as a monetary good and one of the primary investment theses for Bitcoin is as the store of value asset in an increasingly digital world.\n📍 No other digital asset is likely to improve upon Bitcoin as a monetary good because Bitcoin is the most (relative to other digital assets) secure, decentralized, sound digital money.\n📍 One of the greatest characteristics of Bitcoin’s properties is its scarcity - not only is Bitcoin scarce, but unlike gold, it is also provably finite.  There will only ever be 21 million bitcoin.\n📍 No other digital asset possesses an immutable monetary policy on the level of bitcoin - bitcoin's monetary policy may be viewed as the most credible.\n📍 Bitcoin’s scarcity is underpinned by its decentralization and censorship-resistant characteristics. These characteristics are hardcoded into Bitcoin and almost certainly will never be changed because the same people that ascribe value to Bitcoin and own it have no incentive to do so.\n📍 We believe Bitcoin is currently the most secure and decentralized monetary network.\n📍 Bitcoin faces diminishing risks compared to early days and has asymmetric return potential compared to other digital assets.\n\nThey compare Bitocin to the invention of the wheel. But probably the most important part of this that has not been widely discussed is that 'Bitcoin is now the TCP/IP of money'. \n\nLet that sink in.\n\nThe Protocol Wars in the 80's and 90's revolved around selecting the standard protocol for computer and network connectivity, leading to the creation of the Internet.\n\nContenders included OSI, backed by European telephone monopolies, and TCP/IP, supported by grassroots developers. TCP/IP won due to its decentralized nature and focus on running code.\n\nBitcoin is to TCP/IP as a global protocol winner for money, offering the ownership of a scarce digital asset.\n\nIt's like being able to own a piece of the base layer of the internet in the early 90's.\n\nThe game is up - it's over. Bitcoin has won.",
    "date": "2 years ago",
    "likes": 97,
    "comments": 25,
    "impressions": 0,
    "_debug": ""
