    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7108370083709644800",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7108370083709644800/",
    "text": "🚨 Controversial Opinion!! 🚨 \n\nMany won't like this, but I'll say it anyway.\n\nI don't like \nhashtag\n#Apple.\n\nWith the launch of the new \nhashtag\n#iPhone and fanboys worldwide gushing at the opportunity to pay $200 more for the same phone as last year - it reminded me again why really I just don't like this company.\n\nThe iPhone changed the world, but Android offered better and cheaper alternatives and is open source.\n\nI'm actually typing this on a Macbook. It's a stunning piece of hardware and by far the best laptop in terms of performance & battery - but elements of the MacOS drive me insane and I cannot fathom why things like window management, photo browsing and screenshots are so much more complex than windows.\n\nApple brands themselves \"Brave\" for removing ports like the headphone jack and USB-A from laptops, which I find annoying and profit-driven rather than courageous.\n\nWhy give people the ports they need when you can sell them a $59 dongle you probably won't have when you need it most! Genius.\n\nSure the Macbook looks sleeker with just two usb’s - but at the sacrifice of so much!\n\nNow there are great benefits to being deep in the ecosystem - Phone, Laptop, Watch, iPad, TV, etc - but you are committing to spend at least $5k every few years in the refresh cycle.\n\nThey consistently release features that Samsung etc has had for 2 years and call it game-changing.\n\nThey impose artificial restrictions and complicate things for no reason, inventing problems to sell more products.\n\nThey have consistently taken away ports forcing you to buy the adaptors and dongles. They don’t even give you a power brick in the box any more.\n\nSince they were forced to add USB C by the EU - they restricted the base model to USB 2.0 transfer speeds - that's 23 year old technology!! This is insane!!\n\nDespite the potential to make their products more affordable and their ecosystem more open, they continue to lock users in and prioritize profits.\n\nApple excels in providing value and profit for their shareholders, but as a consumer, that's not what I seek. \n\nI don't like Steve Jobs either. Read the books and watch the documentaries they all show he was un unbelievable asshole. Yes he as a visionary but that's no excuse it in my book.\n\nI just bought a new phone last week from a company called OnePlus - I’ve been using them since 2015. It's just as good (or in my opinion significantly better) than the iPhone - and costs $600. Half the price of the new iPhone.\n\nIt is also highly customizable with super useful shortcuts that I would miss on an iPhone. Mainly the have fast charge which is literally 4 times the speed of an iPhone.\n\nI'd much rather give my money to the company making great products at a fair price who try to give more value to customer, than the one that consistently raises prices while delivering mediocre innovation.\n\nAny time I raise these issues with fanboys I get told they 'think different' and I don't understand. I'm sure this will be no different.\n\nSo what am I missing?",
    "date": "2 years ago",
    "likes": 20,
    "comments": 31,
    "impressions": 0,
    "_debug": ""
