    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7096236469379317760",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7096236469379317760/",
    "text": "With all the excitement around Snoop Dogg joining LinkedIn, and so many questions around it, I wanted to share a photo of me with Snoop's son. I worked extensively Cordell and the team - and let me tell you he has an incredible team running his empire who have been consistently pushing the very boundaries of music and technology - and all at the helm of the Doggfather himself.\n\nIt's fantastic to have \nhashtag\n#Snoop on \nhashtag\n#LinkedIn and amazing to see him commenting on posts and responding to comments. So naturally there is a huge buzz around it asking if it is actually him commenting, and exactly to what extent is his knowledge and involvement in Web3?\n\nSo here's my take on it:\n\nNo, I don’t think it's him sitting there answering every comment - he’s got a massive business to run! Please feel free to correct me if I’m wrong Snoop! But perhaps he's in the background sipping on Gin and Juice listening to what’s being said on his new platform of choice.\n\nBut that does not matter! Snoop is the CEO of his empire and he leads his team in the direction and overall strategy. No CEO can do it all himself. He drives the team to execute his ideas - and Snoop has proven himself as a master in the world of both music & business and clearly he’s shown the initiative to become one of the first celebs active on Linkedin. A great sign for the platform.\n\nSo what about Web3? Well, without doubt he has an extremely astute knowledge and understanding as he was truly one of the pioneers in the space. His son and their team are deeply involved, setting records and pushing boundaries.\n\nThey did a $44m NFT drop with Gala games, built a twin of his mansion in Sandbox, and he turned out to be behind the prolific NFT collector Cosmo Medici: https://lnkd.in/dhGU9KYj - to me they are showing they understand the mindset of the new audience and they are leading the charge in the space.\n\nMy favourite example is a clip where Snoop explains why as the new president of death row records, he made the decision to take their music off Spotify and Apple, protesting the pennies artists make from millions of streams. https://lnkd.in/dPkMNVFX\n\nHe's taking control of his music making Death Row an NFT label to give people real ownership of the music. NFTs are misunderstood by many but they have the ability to solve a lot of problems in the music industry and Snoop is doing exactly this, leading the way for others. \n\nSnoop has been pushing the envelope for years with his music and now with emerging technologies affecting the music industry.\n\nKeep it up Dogg and welcome to Linkedin.",
