    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7095055647938912256",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7095055647938912256/",
    "text": "Einstein once said that if he was given an hour to solve a really hard problem, he would spend 55 minutes thinking about the question, and 5 minutes thinking about the answer. In the age of AI and 'Outsourced Intelligence' I think the talent going forward is going to be knowing how to ask the right questions...\n\nI was honoured to be invited onto the Untangling Web3 Podcast with two incredibly esteemed hosts! A Dr. of Philosophy Alec John Burns, PhD, and a University of Cambridge Physics graduate Jack Davies - where we had some amazing chats about Web3 and AI, Metaverse and NFT's.\n\nHighly recommend subscribing to their Podcast and I will be having them on mine soon too - as having minds of this calibre to discuss the future of technology is rare!\n\nEinstein's quote also makes me think about the future of education - in a world where any answer is seconds away, do we need to drill kids to memorise endless facts?\n\nI have a 4 year old son and I love his endless imagination and creativity - I can't wait to unlesh him into an AI to explore every incredible thought and idea.\n\nVery excited to see how the world is going to change in the next few years, in ways that right now we can barely imagine...\n\nThanks Jack and Alec for the great discussion!\n\n\nhashtag\n#einstein\n\nhashtag\n#podcast\n\nhashtag\n#AI",
    "date": "2 years ago",
    "likes": 20,
