    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7090732699337854976/",
    "text": "ChatGPT can now detect cancer apparently! This is wild! \n\nA Reddit user used Bing's image recognition tool and some creative prompting to trick ChatGPT into making a diagnosis on a mole - actually two, one with and one without concern - the answers it gave were spot on, confirmed by a dermatologist in the comments.\n\nNow this is just an experiment for fun FYI. You should absolutely Not use ChatGPT for medical diagnosis..\n\nHowever, for me, this just shows a glimpse into the future.. In time doctors will be able to create apps with large libraries of authenticated scans and maybe soon an app will save you a trip to a specialist.\n\nWould you trust an AI for an initial diagnosis?\n\n\nhashtag\n#chatgpt \n\nhashtag\n#cancer",
