    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7057034288294223872",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7057034288294223872/",
    "text": "Apple are going to put a ChatGPT-like AI inside the next iPhone!\n\n..\n\nThat's my prediction - here's why:\n\nApple have had Siri for years but it's pretty awful - ripe to be replaced by something actually competent.\n\nUnlike Siri, we can talk naturally to LLM's like Chat GPT, and they understand everything. Game changer!\n\nYou'll be able to chat with your phone just like a person, it can interact with apps, complete tasks and be your virtual assistant.\n\nBut Privacy is the big one. No one wants their personal data known by an AI - unless of course all the data is kept 100% secure on your device. \n\nApple are one of the only companies who have proven their commitment to privacy - we certainly would not trust Facebook or even Google not to use this data nefariously.\n\nLLM's are now getting far more efficient and soon they will fit and run fine on a smartphone. \n\nChatGPT is trained on 175 billion parameters, others are 95% smaller and still just as good for most everyday queries.\n\nImagine how it good it will be when it can learn and remember all you're personal details. It can Book flights, make purchases and arrange meetings all automatically and securely.\n\nIt will manage your emails and messages and reply as you - probably all with just your AirPods you won't even need to look at your phone.\n\nLet's see how long it takes them - what do you think?\n\n\nhashtag\n#privacy \nhashtag\n#apple \nhashtag\n#ai",
