    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7048978487096807424",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7048978487096807424/",
    "text": "The Metaverse is Over!! It's Dead!! Pack it up everyone, we’re going home…\n\nWow, that was fast...\n\nIt's only a year since Facebook renamed to Meta and brought the Metaverse to the front of everyone's attention, and already people are bored waiting so have already moved on apparently.\n\nIt reminds me of that famous newspaper headline from the 90's where they proclaim \"Internet may just be a passing fad as millions give up on it\". Transformational technology does not happen overnight.. \n\nWe need to take a step back - what even is the Metaverse? To me, the Metaverse is simply the name we are currently giving to what will become the future evolution of the Internet. And we're still figuring out what that will look like exactly...\n\nA 'Minority Report' style experience would be great but right now that's pretty hard to achieve practically. We still have some significant technological limitations to overcome, both software and hardware.\n\nWe've had VR for some time but it's take-off has been limited as let's face it, no one wants to walk around with a brick strapped to their face..\n\nHowever, Apple are working on a Mixed Reality Headset to be released this year - followed by a pair of normal-looking glasses that will project information into your vision in high-quality MR. \n\nWhen this happens, this is when the metaverse will really start to become mainstream in my opinion. Others will flood in and very quickly we’ll have the information from our phones discreetly in our vision, or when needed, providing an immersive and interactive experience for entertainment, learning and work.\n\nBut it won’t just stop there -  we can go to a whole other level. I have a friend who's working on a contact lens, that gets inserted into your eye in a 5-minute operation just like Cataract surgery, and it has a 4k tv built in so you'll be able to experience the metaverse in your own eyes. It connects to your phone and is powered by blinking\n\n<ming-blown.jpg>\n\nI'm not kidding - it's totally real and a few years away! Just imagine being able to watch a movie with your eyes closed - or use your full computer without a monitor - you'll just see one like it really was there in front of you.\n\nPlug that into Elon Musk's Neuralink brain-computer-interface - and tap into an AI to turbocharge your mind - and one can only imagine the possibilities and how different things will become.\n\nWe all know the next few years is going to change our lives and the world dramatically - especially with the rapid advancement of AI LLM’s. So we need to think about what we want the Internet to become when this happens.\n\nRight now, there are thousands of companies working on building amazing tech - incredible metaverses, products, services and experiences for this new world. Like the Crypto Winters, this time is for building and let’s forget the media hype.\n\nThe Metaverse isn't dead. It’s only just been born!\n\n\nhashtag\n#metaverse\n\nhashtag\n#mixedreality\n\nhashtag\n#augmentedreality",
    "date": "2 years ago",
    "likes": 51,
    "comments": 32,
    "impressions": 0,
    "_debug": ""
