    "urn": "urn:li:activity:7046820331457589249",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7046820331457589249/",
    "text": "Visualising the advancement of AI over 12 months - in 5 Pictures. Check out the last one - just breathtaking!!\n\nThis is Midjourney v1 released in March 2022, through to Midjourney v5 in March 2023. The rate of improvement is astonishing.\n\nThe Prompt was \"Red haired woman wearing sunglasses standing with the Statue of Liberty in the background, photograph, 35mm film\".\n\nIt's gone from strange wonky looking art, to proper photo realistic pictures, in just a year. \n\nWe've all seen the photos of the Pope in the big white Jacket made by AI that fooled the internet - or the politicians getting arrested - and no doubt there will be many more fooled. \nhashtag\n#AI can now create pictures indistinguishable from reality in seconds - as if we didn't have enough of a problem with fake news. How will this affect propaganda or the US elections? Will regulation do anything?\n\nI've been an avid photographer for a long time - and always had a passion for graphic design (despite being terrible at it) - but it's concerning how quickly \nhashtag\n#Midjourney and \nhashtag\n#dalle2 will disrupt these industries\n\nMainly though - Chat GPT, Bard, PaLM, LLaMA and the others are going to see similar rapid advancement and I'm so excited to see the possibilities.\n\nIt's going to be one hell of a year!",
    "date": "2 years ago",
    "likes": 28,
