    "urn": "urn:li:activity:6934007516729085952",
    "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:6934007516729085952/",
    "text": "So, that really happened... \nhashtag\n#luna got nuked.\n\nThe price fell from $116 in April to just a penny on Thursday, wiping out a market cap of $40B within a few short days. \n\nHow?\n\nWell, they experienced the equivalent of a bank-run. \n\nHere's what happened:\n\nSomeone (unclear who) started dumping huge amounts of Luna stablecoin, \nhashtag\n#ust , into the market. Through on-chain analysis we can see there were two entities that, in a 24-hour period, sold over $400 million of UST. \n\nThe stablecoin's $ peg started to wobble and caused cascading liquidation effect as UST holders rushed for the exit. What started as a short attack on UST/$ peg turned into a full fledge panic. Everyone wanted to trade in their UST.\n\nLuna Foundation Guard (LFG) started aggressively unloading their reserves and buying UST in an effort to save the stablecoin. \n\nBut the $3B of reserves in BTC was just a drop in the bucket and did nothing to stop the bleeding. If anything, LFG's sell pressure just tanked the rest of the market driving BTC below $30k. \n\nUltimately, the peg derailed and Luna went broke burning through its reserves. \n\nSo what's the point?\n\nThe attackers had an open short BTC 100k position of borrowed bitcoin. Once LFG was desperately selling their BTC at a sharp discount the attackers were able to settle their short position with far cheaper BTC, pocketing the difference of $800M.\n\nI'm sure a lot more info will come to light in the coming months. These numbers are just too massive to hide. Meanwhile, this is being called a \"brilliant\", George Soros style attack.\n\nAt this scale, it's definitely a first in crypto.\n\n\nhashtag\n#TerraUSD \nhashtag\n#bitcoin \nhashtag\n#crypto \nhashtag\n#cryptocurrencies \nhashtag\n#money \nhashtag\n#business \nhashtag\n#dollar",
    "date": "3 years ago",
    "likes": 6,
    "comments": 0,
